TABLES in html
table are used to display data in tabular form
table tag
th - table header it is used to define header cell in a table
td - table data it is used to define data cell in a table
tr - table row it is used to define a row in a table
difference between th and td is th is bold and centered by default where as td is normal text left aligned by default
caption tag is used to add title to the table
basic structures
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <head>
        <title>Table Example</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <table border="1">
            <caption>Student Scores</caption>
            <tr>
                <th>Name</th>
                <th>Subject</th>
                <th>Score</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Alice</td>
                <td>Math</td>
                <td>95</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Bob</td>
                <td>Science</td>
                <td>88</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </body>

rowspan and colspan attributes
rowspan attribute is used to merge two or more rows in a table vertically
colspan attribute is used to merge two or more columns in a table horizontally
example:
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
    <head>
        <title>Table with Rowspan and Colspan</title>
    </head>
    <body>
        <table border="1">
            <tr>
                <th rowspan="2">Name</th>
                <th colspan="2">Scores</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <th>Math</th>
                <th>Science</th>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Alice</td>
                <td>95</td>
                <td>90</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>Bob</td>
                <td>88</td>
                <td>85</td>
            </tr>
        </table>
    </body>


